    "setTail": "Main-thread long-task cooldowns repeatedly reset fresh-frame confirmation. Slow detector inputs could also exceed the fixed outline-age window before three samples completed. White sleeves could keep the front detector class and miss the confirmation burst. Quiet scans ran too often because cached pixel checks lowered the detector cost estimate; localized changes after idle could lose the ROI path.",
    "fix": "Remove the long-task cooldown; retain input/manual-read guards and inference duty budget. Confirm with three fresh still, sharp, matching pixel frames using a bounded detector-age window, including same-class white Set transitions. Use localized ROI after idle, retain full-scan fallback, and exclude cached pixel checks from detector cost. Keep quiet empty-field retries, at least two seconds apart, so a transient miss recovers."
  },
